      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for pointing that out — that null check was effectively useless, so I removed it.\n\nI confirmed that parseTerminusPDRs() is the only place that populates entityAuxiliaryNamesTbl, and it already null-checks each entry before inserting it. So by the time this lambda runs, every element is guaranteed non-null.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/pldm/blob/42532e4f8085d264c36c0c1eafad15306c7f3e42/platform-mc/terminus.cpp#L204\n\nI\u0027ve added a comment documenting that invariant, so if entityAuxiliaryNames is ever null in the future, the program will crash right here — making it much easier to pinpoint where the invariant was broken, instead of silently masking the bug behind a redundant check.",
